inode/system — `/`, and the outermost window.

The TYPE is ordinary. The outermost WINDOW is the special case, and in
exactly one respect: its chrome belongs to the host — the macOS title
bar and menu bar, the browser's tab and toolbar, the iPad's furniture.
Its body is children, like any container, and the tree is untouched.

A nested emca opens its own `/` with this same manager and ORDINARY
emca chrome, because its parent is an emca window rather than the host.

The manager owns a writable child as well as the composition — layout's
first entry, `/` itself — rendered as a left pane in the browser and a
collapsible sidebar on macOS and iPadOS, where collapsing it IS
`minimise` on that window.
